message: "If you use this code, data, or paper, please cite it as below."
title: "Communication Causes Price Coordination in LLM Seller Agents; Public Logging and Audits Suppress It, Unevenly Across Models"
authors:
  - family-names: Lux
    given-names: Alois
date-released: 2026-09-21
url: "https://github.com/alu-developer/ai-agent-price-collusion"
license: "MIT"
license-url-data-and-paper: "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/alu-developer/ai-agent-price-collusion"
keywords:
  - algorithmic collusion
  - large language models
  - multi-agent systems
  - AI safety
  - price coordination
abstract: >
  A controlled, pre-registered study of whether letting LLM-based seller
  agents exchange short cheap-talk messages causes price coordination in a
  repeated Bertrand-style market, and whether a permanent public log or
  random audits suppress it. Tested identically across two model families
  (GPT-5.6-luna, Claude Haiku 4.5). Full raw data, code, and paper included.
